---
import { ShieldCheck, EyeOff, Scale } from 'lucide-react';
---

<section id="trust" class="py-20 lg:py-28 border-t border-border-custom bg-bg-secondary/20">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-12 lg:gap-8 items-center">
      
      <!-- Left Column: Copy -->
      <div class="lg:col-span-7 flex flex-col items-center lg:items-start text-center lg:text-left reveal">
        <h2 class="font-display text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-text-main mb-6">
          100% Local. <br class="hidden sm:inline" />
          <span class="text-gold">100% Open Source.</span>
        </h2>
        
        <p class="font-body text-sm sm:text-base text-text-muted mb-8 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
          Because Warp Transfer bundles and executes the official Android Debug Bridge (`adb.exe`) to communicate with your phone over USB/Wi-Fi, standard Windows Defender or antivirus products may occasionally flag the executable. This section outlines our core security tenets.
        </p>

        <!-- Bullet List -->
        <div class="space-y-6 max-w-2xl">
          
          <div class="flex items-start space-x-3.5 text-left">
            <div class="flex h-9 w-9 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-gold-glow border border-gold/20 text-gold mt-0.5">
              <EyeOff className="h-4 w-4" />
            </div>
            <div>
              <h4 class="font-display text-base font-bold text-text-main">Zero Telemetry & Tracking</h4>
              <p class="font-body text-xs sm:text-sm text-text-muted mt-1 leading-relaxed">
                Warp Transfer does not collect, log, or send any user statistics. The app operates completely locally on your PC and device with no external server queries.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="flex items-start space-x-3.5 text-left">
            <div class="flex h-9 w-9 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-gold-glow border border-gold/20 text-gold mt-0.5">
              <Scale className="h-4 w-4" />
            </div>
            <div>
              <h4 class="font-display text-base font-bold text-text-main">MIT Licensed Transparency</h4>
              <p class="font-body text-xs sm:text-sm text-text-muted mt-1 leading-relaxed">
                Warp Transfer is fully open-source. Developers can review the complete codebase, audit our parallel worker thread loop, or build the binary directly from source files.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Right Column: Visual Shield Card -->
      <div class="lg:col-span-5 flex justify-center reveal">
        <div class="w-full max-w-sm rounded-2xl border border-border-custom bg-bg-secondary/40 p-6 flex flex-col items-center justify-center text-center">
          <div class="flex h-14 w-14 items-center justify-center rounded-2xl bg-gold-glow border border-gold/30 text-gold mb-6 animate-pulse">
            <ShieldCheck className="h-7 w-7" />
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-display text-base font-bold text-text-main mb-2">Platform Security Checked</h3>
          <p class="font-body text-xs text-text-muted leading-relaxed mb-4 max-w-[240px]">
            Warp Transfer runs strictly on local loopbacks and ADB pipes. No telemetry, no background trackers.
          </p>
          <a href="https://github.com/tahsanahmmed25/warp-transfer/blob/main/LICENSE" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="font-body text-[10px] text-gold hover:underline">
            Read License Agreement
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>
